      "paper_id": "doi:10.1007/s10640-026-01091-4",
      "sequence": 1,
      "source_sequence": 44,
      "article_type": "research-article",
      "title_en": "Director Appointments, Boardroom Networks, and Firm Environmental Performance",
      "title_cn": "董事任命、董事会网络与企业环境绩效",
      "authors": [
        "Mingyuan Chen",
        "Dakshina G. De Silva",
        "Aurelie Slechten"
      ],
      "abstract_en": "Using BoardEx (2000–2017), we create a dynamic network connecting firms and board directors in the United States. We use the Environmental Protection Agency’s Toxics Release Inventory to measure environmental performance at the director and firm-level. We first examine how candidates’ environmental performance and networks affect their probability to be appointed to the board. We find that firms are likely to appoint influential directors with good environmental records and similar characteristics. We then show that directors’ past environmental records affect their current firm’s chemical releases. We address endogeneity concerns related to directors’ appointments and firms’ environmental performance by modeling directors’ network formation.",
      "abstract_cn": "利用BoardEx数据（2000-2017年），我们构建了一个连接美国公司与董事的动态网络。我们使用环境保护署的有毒物质排放清单来衡量董事和公司层面的环境绩效。我们首先考察候选人的环境绩效和网络如何影响他们被任命为董事的概率。我们发现，公司倾向于任命具有良好环境记录和相似特征的有影响力的董事。然后，我们表明董事过去的环境记录会影响他们当前公司的化学物质排放。我们通过模拟董事网络的形成来解决与董事任命和公司环境绩效相关的内生性问题。",
